    "top_frame": "This team doesn't fold when it matters.",
    "what_this_means": "They led after the second inning and never trailed. Two runs came in the second, two more in the fourth. The kind of front-loaded offense that lets you breathe easy. But what made tonight matter was the structure underneath: Nick Pivetta lasted just 3.1 innings, and the bullpen answered. Bradgley Rodriguez, Jason Adam, Adrian Morejon, Mason Miller. Four relievers threw 5.2 clean innings combined. They converted three of eight RISP situations into runs. This is what balanced production looks like. Not dominant, not elegant, just enough leverage at the right moments and nothing to regret after.",
